  "response": "{\"thought\": \"I need to create a story bible for SpaceGame, following the specific constraints provided.\", \"title\": \"The Broken Orbit\", \"description\": \"A pilot's desperate struggle to survive in the lawless fringes of the Aurelia sector.\", \"campaign_pitch\": \"You are an independent pilot struggling with debt. You must navigate trade routes and pirate threats to earn enough for a new ship.\", \"campaign_story_summary\": \"The Aurelia system is plagued by illegal smuggling. You start as a broke pilot in a scrapyard station. Kaelen offers you your first contract. A Reaver scout ship attacks during the delivery. You survive but realize the sector is unstable. Your survival depends on your ability to negotiate and fight.\", \"factions\": [\n    {\"name\": \"Zenith\", \"description\": \"A high-tech corporation seeking order through strict regulation.\"},\n    {\"name\": \"Aurelia\", \"description\": \"A loose confederation of miners and independent traders.\"},\n    {\"name\": \"Vanguard\", \"description\": \"A militant group dedicated to purging pirate activity.\"}\n], \"npcs\": [\n    {\"name\": \"Kaelen\", \"role\": \"Broker\", \"description\": \"A fixer who handles contracts for the local trade routes.\", \"notes\": \"She knows more than she admits, but her true motives are hidden.\"}\n], \"world_building\": \"The system is a hub of illegal smuggling and desperate trade. The Reaver threat is constant but poorly understood.\", \"gameplay_s_requirements\": \"Mining, salvage, delivery, combat, station services, rumors, and gate exploration are all supported.\", \"mission_1_title\": \"First Blood\", \"mission_1_description\": \"Intercept a smuggler's cargo. A Reaver scout ship will intercept you during the flight.\", \"enemy_type_1\": \"Reaver Scout\", \"starter_hostile_ship_count\": \"1\", \"mechanics_integration\": \"The player must navigate gates, mine asteroids, and trade with various factions.\", \"lore_thought\": \"The local lore is centered on the immediate survival of independent pilots.\"}",
